            <ArticleTitle>Chest pain in an adult with truncus arteriosus communis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>272-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We present a case of an adult patient with truncus arteriosus communis and secondary pulmonary hypertension. He had chest pain and sudden death due to cardiac tamponade caused by intramural-limited dissection and rupture of the common trunk.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
